Defect found and fixed this phase, inherited from Phase 1:
  stepToNextHeel lands exactly on a vertex, which the Phase 1 resolver read as
  still inside the previous segment. That method therefore never registered a
  heel crossing - no onTurn, no announcement, no checkpoint. Phase 1 specs
  passed because they asserted resulting progress only, never the events.

  Fixed by separating heel crossing (arrival, from < b <= to) from segment
  index (segmented >= boundary, non-segmented > boundary). The asymmetry
  mirrors the two pointer paths it parallels, and the non-segmented
  conservatism is load-bearing: on [100,100,5], resting exactly on the final
  vertex reaches 97.56%, and treating that as having entered the final segment
  would grant unlock with none of it traversed.

The core engine is feature-complete for this track. Phase 3 consumes it.

